  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14097897/assets/8d7ceac8c936a745ae79f71844a6d1a74175b1b97a2a497588d34c9ff988cdf9.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
  "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $\u2202A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $\u2202A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14097897/assets/c0e6ef400b15c54264a400af99bef64c3bb5aeb7ceadbdd599375c0f1e0d3642.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-\u2202A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14097897/assets/8c5bbdfca6736194791f834ab4aadb03a30e3f116e89ffd5a7ea3e0104708ae4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x}.\n$$",
